# Feature-Sliced Design Architecture Rules

## Project Structure

`apps/web` uses **Feature-Sliced Design (FSD)**. Layer hierarchy:

```
app → pages → widgets → features → entities → shared
```

Layers import only downward. Per layer (except shared): slices → segments. Enforced by ESLint
(`apps/web/linter/rules/restricted-imports-rule.ts`).

**Layers:**
- **app/** — bootstrap config, providers, routes, root component
- **pages/** — routed page components
- **widgets/** — composite UI blocks (e.g. the den world, the details panel)
- **features/** — user interactions (toggle sound, switch skin, ...)
- **entities/** — domain models (agent, room, achievement): types, stores, adapters
- **shared/** — UI kit, lib helpers, api clients (WebSocket), config

**Segments:** `ui/` (components), `model/` (signals stores, types, pure logic), `api/` (transport — internal to the slice), `lib/` (helpers).

## UI kit boundary

- `@spartan-ng/*` may be imported **only** inside `src/shared/**`.
- Every primitive is wrapped in a `src/shared/ui/<name>/` component (`den-*` selector, own styles) and exported from `@shared`.
- Upper layers never use Spartan directives directly — if a wrapper is missing, add it to `shared/ui` first.

## Import Rules

**Cross-layer — single-word aliases only:**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { DenButton, cn } from '@shared';
import { AgentStore, type AgentView } from '@entities';

// ❌ WRONG
import { DenButton } from '@shared/ui';
import { AgentStore } from '@entities/agent';
import { BrnDialog } from '@spartan-ng/brain/dialog'; // outside shared
```

**Intra-layer — absolute paths from `src/`:**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { DenWorldRoom } from 'src/widgets/den-world/ui/den-world-room';
```

Relative imports (`./`, `../`) are forbidden. Shared contracts with the collector come from `@agent-den/contracts`.

## Public API Exports

Every layer, slice, and segment MUST have `index.ts` re-exporting public API. Use explicit named exports
(`export { X } from '...'`), NOT `export *`. Export only what consumers need. Index files use absolute `src/` paths.

```typescript
// Layer root: src/pages/index.ts
export { DenPage } from 'src/pages/den';

// Slice: src/entities/agent/index.ts
export { AgentStore, type AgentView } from 'src/entities/agent/model';
```

## When Creating New Code

1. Pick correct layer
2. Create or use slice
3. Organize by segments (ui, model, api, lib)
4. Add `index.ts` at each level
5. Export only public API via index
6. Use single-word imports from other layers

## Example Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts
├── styles.css
├── app/
│   ├── index.ts
│   ├── app.ts
│   ├── app.config.ts
│   └── app.routes.ts
├── pages/
│   ├── index.ts
│   └── den/
│       ├── index.ts
│       └── ui/den-page.ts
├── widgets/
│   └── den-world/
│       ├── index.ts
│       └── ui/ (den-world.ts, den-world.css, den-world-room.ts)
├── features/
│   └── toggle-sound/
├── entities/
│   └── agent/
│       ├── index.ts
│       ├── api/ (agent-socket.ts)
│       └── model/ (agent-store.ts, types.ts)
└── shared/
    ├── index.ts
    ├── ui/
    │   ├── index.ts
    │   └── button/ (den-button.ts, den-button.css)
    └── lib/
        ├── index.ts
        └── cn.ts
```
